Start Here

This repository explores hypothetical ideas involving backward time travel, spacetime geometry, human transportation, Temporal GIS, causal modeling, and the ethical limits of interventions affecting people or historical events.

The project combines two distinct aims:

Personal aim: Preserve the hope of learning from past mistakes, gaining closure, avoiding preventable harm, and pursuing meaningful goals in education, relationships, creativity, and everyday life.

Research aim: Invite independent assessment of speculative ideas related to spacetime, causality, information preservation, simulation, and safety.

These aims are related, but neither establishes that backward time travel is physically possible.

