Scientific Status

Backward time travel to the past and human teleportation have not been demonstrated. Quantum teleportation does not transport a person or provide faster-than-light communication. Warp-drive metrics and wormhole concepts do not by themselves demonstrate that a usable device can be built.

Code, equations, diagrams, and simulations in this repository must not be treated as proof of physical feasibility. Any claim of feasibility would require reproducible evidence, independent scientific review, realistic energy and stability analysis, causal-consistency analysis, and rigorous safety assessment.

Mission Interpretation

Any date or time described in a mission document is a proposed scenario or historical record, not evidence that a mission launched, that a message was transmitted through time, or that an intervention occurred.

A proposed review request does not authorize experiments on people, access to private records, surveillance, or actions without appropriate consent and legal authorization.

Preservation and Version History

The repository is intended to be preserved and reviewed as a record of ideas and research questions. Readers are encouraged to:

